%N A071091 Number of lozenge tilings of a hexagon with side lengths 2n, 2n+3, 2n, 2n+3, 2n, 2n+3, with the middle unit triangle removed from each of the three longer sides.
%D A071091 James Propp, Enumeration of matchings: problems and progress, pp. 255-291 in L. J. Billera et al., eds, New Perspectives in Algebraic Combinatorics, Cambridge, 1999 (see Problem 2).
%H A071091 Seiichi Manyama, <a href="/A071091/b071091.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..26</a>
%H A071091 M. Ciucu et al., <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/math/9912053">Enumeration of lozenge tilings of hexagons with a central triangular hole</a>, arXiv:math/9912053 [math.CO], 1999.
%H A071091 Theresia Eisenkölbl, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/math/9712261">Rhombus Tilings of a Hexagon with Three Fixed Border Tiles</a>, 1998.
%H A071091 James Propp, <a href="http://faculty.uml.edu/jpropp/update.pdf">Update on Enumeration of Matchings</a>, 2009.
%H A071091 James Propp, <a href="https://library.slmath.org/books/Book38/files/propp.pdf">Enumeration of Matchings: Problems and Progress</a>, in L. J. Billera et al. (eds.), New Perspectives in Algebraic Combinatorics, MSRI Publications, Vol. 38, Cambridge Univ. Press, 1999, pp. 255-291.
%F A071091 a(n) = (n+1)^3 * (3*n+1) * (3*n+2)^2 * pochhammer(n+2, 2*n)^6 * S(2*n)^3 * S(6*n+2) / S(4*n+2)^3 where S(n) = A000178(n) = Product_{k=0..n} k! [Corollary 2 of Eisenkölbl]. - _Sean A. Irvine_, Jun 27 2024
%e A071091 From _Seiichi Manyama_, Jul 28 2026: (Start)
%e A071091 For n = 1, the region has side lengths 2, 5, 2, 5, 2, 5. In the following boundary diagram, each x marks the position of a removed unit triangle in the middle of one of the three longer sides:
